  "date": "December 10 1990",
  "content": "Suddenly I was in what I call the white room. I found myself above looking down at my mangled self under the collapsed air stair. No voices, no ghostly forms just a very pleasant experience. Then my name being called by my landlord - who told me later that when he walked into the hanger and saw me mangled under the pile of steel, he threw up. He said that he hadn't seen anything like that since WWII. I was transported to the Hospital by helicopter for nine and a half hours of surgery and a five month stay in the hospital.",
